# ycal-website (Vite · React Router)

## Stack (source of truth)

Vite ~6, React ~19, `react-router-dom` ~7, TypeScript. Behavior and plugin choices follow [Vite](https://vite.dev/) and [React Router](https://reactrouter.com/).

## Obligatory placement under `src/`

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|--------|-----------|------------------|
| Route components | `src/pages/*.tsx` | One exported page per logical URL; assemble layout + SEO + content sections |
| App shell | `src/App.tsx` | `Routes`, wrappers, basename alignment with deployment |
| Entry | `src/main.tsx` | `createRoot`, `BrowserRouter`/provider wiring only |
| Layout / chrome | `src/components/` | `Layout`, navigation, reusable sections — not duplicate headers per page |
| SEO bridge | `src/seo/` | JSON-LD, `document`/meta mutations, basename helpers consumed by routing and build pipeline |
| Build-time constants | `src/config.ts`, `vite.config.ts`, `scripts/` | Public URLs, env expectations; keep drift between basename and GH Pages deploy path impossible by sharing helpers |

Thin `App.tsx` / `pages/`: if a page accumulates fetching, document effects, **and** large JSX trees, lift **logic** into a small hook under `components/`/`hooks/`/`seo/` consistent with neighboring code.

## Routing and URLs

1. Prefer React Router primitives (`Routes`, `Route`, hooks) aligned with [`routerBasename` / basename](https://reactrouter.com/en/main/router-components/browser-router) conventions already in tree.
2. New routes get a **`Route`**, a **`src/pages`** entry, nav links updated in layout, and any SEO/meta updates centralized in `seo/` helpers so `build` still produces consistent HTML artifacts.

## Component reuse on the marketing site

- Shared chrome (site header/footer, legal boilerplate wrappers) belongs in `src/components/`; pages pass content or shallow props only.
- For repeated marketing blocks (“feature row”, testimonial layouts), introduce one parameterized component rather than duplicating JSX across Home/Privacy/etc.
- When adding assets, prefer `public/` for static blobs and coherent naming; avoid inlined huge assets in TS when a static URL suffices.

## SEO and builds

1. Canonical tags, OG/Twitter, title/description, structured data (`jsonLd`, `documentMeta`) must live in **`src/seo/`** or be imported from there so `scripts/finish-seo.mjs` and SSR-less hosting assumptions stay coherent.
2. Relative links and anchors must behave under the deployed base path (`BrowserRouter basename` parity). Test with `vite build` + `preview` rather than guessing.

## Verification for this package

Touching routes, basename, SEO, or `index.html`:

- Run `yarn lint` and `yarn build`.
- If navigation or deep links changed, confirm `yarn preview` for key paths (home, privacy, terms) under the basename.
